#
# To capture more, drive the server over stdio and record what it sends back:
# initialize, then `initialized` and a `didOpen`, then wait for the
# `$/progress` end of its indexing token before asking anything — a definition
# request that arrives first is answered `null`, which looks like a real answer
# and is not one. Only server-to-client messages are worth capturing here; the
# client half of this file is ours either way.
#
# Servers still wanted, per §8.5: pyright, gopls, and any editor's own
# initialize params.
